        "id": "CA18/2/14/22",
        "title": "Nent Haggs Optimisation",
        "description": "This contract was awarded following a further competition from the Mining Remediation Authority's Research and Development Dynamic Purchasing System Lot 2\r\n\r\nThis requirement is for ongoing treatment optimisation at Nent Haggs Mine Water Treatment Works. \r\n\r\nThe package of works is to be phased over a four year programme, \r\n\r\nThe site has been operational since September 2024, with Treatment Pond 1 (TP1) brought online in accordance with planning conditions. \r\n\r\nContaminated mine water has been entering TP1 at a controlled flow rate. Since commissioning, the passive treatment system has successfully removed an dissolved zinc from the inflowing mine water. \r\n\r\nThe next stage of commissioning involves a structured optimisation programme aimed at enhancing treatment performance at Nent Haggs and informing the development of future passive mine water treatment systems for the Mining Remediation Authority.",
